"""Flytoget Type 78 (CAF Oaris, 4 cars), cab car MC2 facing right and the end of MI2. docs/TRAIN_ART.md.

Who runs it (checked 2026-10-22): Flytoget runs Type 71 and Type 78 side by side on FLY1 and FLY2. Entur's live
vehicle positions (https://api.entur.io/realtime/v1/gtfs-rt/vehicle-positions?datasource=FLT, 2026-10-22 17:06 CEST)
listed 12 sets in service: 8 Type 71 (71-02/03/04/07/09/10/13/14) and 4 Type 78 (78-02/05/07/08); each vehicle id names
its set, so the app can tell which type a train is. Norske tog's fleet pages list 15 Type 71 and 8 Type 78
(norsketog.no/tog/motorvognsett/type-71 and /type-78). This file draws the Type 78; flytoget71.py the Type 71.

Drawn: cab car MC2 (cab facing right; Norske tog draws it so, no mirroring) and the end of MI2. MC2 is MC1 mirrored.

Sources (retrieved 2026-10-22):
- Norske tog side elevations, one SVG per car: https://www.norsketog.no/uploads/trains/filled/motor-coach/Type78/78-MC2.svg,
  78-MI2.svg, 78-MC1.svg (page https://www.norsketog.no/tog/motorvognsett/type-78). Its greys and orange are Flytoget's
  livery layers (checked against the photos below), so they are used as the livery.
- Side-on photo, Norske tog "Oaris_Flytoget" (test run in Germany, 2019; same livery as in service),
  https://www.norsketog.no/imager/images/Tog/Type78/15257/Oaris_Flytoget_e1c911f2f3d0fd466fe982bf5a56cab5.jpg (2400 px):
  whole MC1, long lens. Rectified with 12 door/window corners (rms 3 cm), then overlaid.
- Side-on photo of both cab ends, Flickr 54211015376 (Stale Naess, "Flytoget AS", sets 78003 and 78105 nose to nose), 1024 px: cab, orange line,
  diagonal stripe, windscreen. Close range, so only side-surface features are compared (the nose top is 3D).
- In service in the current livery: Flickr 55240227085 (Skoyen 2026-04-25), 54167766925 (78008, Oslo S),
  54210112292 (3/4, colours, bogie). no.wikipedia "Type 78 (motorvognsett)" and "CAF Oaris": 4 cars, 102 m, wheels 920 mm.
Scale: 71.0 px/m, checked three ways: roof (y 137.4) to rail (445.8) 308.4 px = 4.343 m (Norske tog: height 4343 mm);
the four cars' drawings end to end 7263 px = 102.3 m (Norske tog: 102 250 mm); the door and window pattern of MC1
fits the Oaris photo with a projective fit to under 1 photo px (22 points).
Elevation px (MC2): nose tip x 1877.0, roof top y 137.4, skirt bottom y 426.7, body end x 32.8 (car 25.98 m), bellows
1.8-32.8 plus MI2's 1722.5-1753.4 (gangway 0.87 m).
- windows y 246.6-301.7 at x 105.7-227.9, 254.7-376.9, 647.2-739.9, 773.0-865.7, 903.9-996.6, 1029.6-1122.3, 1395.5-1517.7;
  narrow windows by the doors 406.1-439.0, 585.7-611.5, 1159.3-1185.2, 1331.8-1364.7 (y 238.9-317.2).
- doors 456.1-571.2 and 1196.8-1311.8 (orange frame, y 205.4-389.3), door windows y 240.5-298.9; steps y 386.9-405.8.
- cab side window 1589.5-1633.4 x 232.9-274.0; cab joint x 1547.8; roof/side line y 178.5; skirt from y 381.1.
- livery layers (elevation paths 2-7, 19): silver body; graphite roof down to y 178.5, a silver strip to 194.3, graphite
  to 222.3, silver with the orange dashes (y 224-228.5) to the window band 232.9-317.2 (graphite, its front end one
  slanted straight edge), silver to 381.1, graphite skirt; at the cab a graphite surround round the side window, and
  the orange line from the dashes' height round the cab window, down the nose and back along y 375-381.
  Photo 54211015376 confirms each band, the light diagonal between the cab surround and the band, and the solid
  orange running 30 px (0.4 m) behind the cab joint before the dashes start.
- forward of the cab joint the graphite top is the windscreen: black glass in the Oaris photo, glass reflecting the
  street in 54211015376; it's drawn as glass on every version.
- bogies: wheel centres x 179.9, 365.0, 1404.0, 1589.1 (y 410.5), axles 2.61 m; frames drawn over the wheels as the
  elevation shows them; wheels 0.92 m (CAF; the elevation draws them 0.99 m).
Overlay checks (scratchpad trains/flytoget): on the rectified Oaris photo every door, window, the orange line and
the dashes coincide (rms 3 cm); on 54211015376 the cab window, plate, orange line and stripe coincide at 96 px/m.
Not drawn: pantograph (on MI2, out of view), headlights (front face), lettering, logos, numbers.
Unverified: the nose top outline (both photos put it 0.2 m higher, but both are 3D views of a curved nose; the
elevation, right everywhere else, is kept); the exact edge of the windscreen glass inside the graphite top.
"""
import os
import re
import sys

sys.path.insert(0, os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__)))
from lib import Drawing, main  # noqa: E402

FT = 'flytoget'
PXM = 71.0  # elevation px per metre
EN, ER, EB = 1877.0, 137.4, 426.7  # MC2 nose tip x, roof top y, underside of the skirt y (elevation px)
MC2_END, MI2_END = 32.8, 1722.5  # body ends at the gangway: MC2's rear, MI2's end next to MC2
GANGWAY = 62.0  # MC2's bellows (1.8-32.8) plus MI2's (1722.5-1753.4)
d = Drawing(car_m=(EN - MC2_END) / PXM, body_m=(EB - ER) / PXM, gangway_m=GANGWAY / PXM, liveries=[FT])
M, ROOF, BASE, TIP, REAR, S = d.M, d.ROOF, d.BASE, d.TIP, d.REAR, d.SECOND_END
K = M / PXM


def ex(px):
    """MC2 elevation x (px) to drawing x."""
    return TIP - (EN - px) * K


def ex2(px):
    """MI2 elevation x (px) to drawing x: its gangway end sits at the start of the gangway."""
    return S - (MI2_END - px) * K


def ey(py):
    return ROOF + (py - ER) * K


def f(py):
    """Elevation y (px) as a fraction of body height, for the kit's windows."""
    return (py - ER) / (EB - ER)


def epath(dstr, X=ex):
    """An elevation path (absolute M/L/H/V/C/Z only, as Norske tog's SVGs are) in drawing coordinates."""
    out, cmd, nums = [], None, []

    def flush():
        if cmd is None:
            return
        if cmd == 'Z':
            out.append('Z')
        elif cmd == 'H':
            out.append('H' + ' '.join(f'{X(n):.1f}' for n in nums))
        elif cmd == 'V':
            out.append('V' + ' '.join(f'{ey(n):.1f}' for n in nums))
        else:
            out.append(cmd + ' '.join(f'{X(nums[i]):.1f},{ey(nums[i + 1]):.1f}' for i in range(0, len(nums), 2)))

    for tok in re.findall(r'[MLHVCZ]|-?\d*\.?\d+(?:e-?\d+)?', dstr):
        if tok in 'MLHVCZ':
            flush()
            cmd, nums = tok, []
        else:
            nums.append(float(tok))
    flush()
    return ''.join(out)


